      "content": "Even though the drinks seem low, the combination of electrolytes helps balance your body's overall fluid and mineral status, which is key for recovery. Ingesting 2000mg of potassium chloride at once is a massive, concentrated dose that can shock your system and cause dangerous imbalances. Your kidneys will process it, but a sudden large influx can disrupt heart and muscle function much faster than your body can handle. Please stick to gradual, balanced rehydration to safely support your recovery.",
